i'll miss harry's world so much  welcome back to another video fellow  potterheads the harry potter cast has  spoken many times about how spectacular  the 10 years on set of the franchise was  for them  but did you know that a lot of these  actors were so close to not landing the  role  the majority of the cast don't have your  traditional audition story  and you'll never believe how some of  these actors landed a part in the film  ready to hear the stories accio year  2000  ten-year-old daniel had no idea how much  the harry potter producers wanted him  for this role  his dad actually knew some of the  filmmakers from having worked with them  in his everyday job as a literary agent  that didn't stop them from rejecting  their offers to have daniel audition  though  in the early days harry potter was  actually supposed to be filmed in  america  and the actors were asked to sign on for  all movies at just 10 years old  you know you would sign up for the  entire series and  it was all to be filmed in america dan's  parents thought that that was a little  too disruptive to their son's life  little did they know what would happen  but then one trip to the theater turned  that all around  daniel's parents took seeing the harry  potter screenwriters as a sign  and voila i don't believe in fate but  very fortunately my parents do  he went on to audition and found out he  got the part while taking a bath  to this day dan claims it was luck and  the fact that he loved what he was doing  that landed him the part  dragon egg uh-huh is that what it is  yeah  rupert's audition story is a true  testament to how similar he actually is  to ron weasley  he sent not one but two audition tapes  he never received a response from the  first one  so decided to make another one and take  it to the next level with  a wrap i thought i did a wrap how i  wanted to pay rome  that got the casting department's  attention and after multiple auditions  he was officially ron weasley something  doesn't make sense  back in 2011 he even performed the wrap  take a listen  hello there my name is rupert  i hope you like this and don't think i  stink emma watson had close to no  experience when she was cast in harry  potter  the casting directors from the film had  visited schools in london looking for  the perfect hermione  my school got an invitation to like get  16 of us from the school of the ages  around  11. they obviously loved her because  they called her in for a proper audition  six more to be exact and then finally  offered her the part  emma still believes that she got the  role because of her determination  even without experience how hermione of  her  jk rowling thought so too even if she  originally mentioned that emma was a  little  too pretty to play hermione shut up if  phil just comes around the corner any  second now  the theme of matthew lewis's neville  audition is 100  dedication he waited in line for about  five hours with his mom at an open  audition just for the chance to show his  talent  he was a huge fan of harry potter and  needed a role  just been so so fortunate to be in a  project like that but a huge fan of the  books  even after his mom tried convincing him  just to head home  he was determined to reach the front of  the line and he did  believe it or not tom felton wasn't in  the market to play draco malfoy  he originally auditioned for both harry  potter and ron weasley  he obviously didn't get those lead roles  but we're pretty sure  him playing draco instead was the  perfect decision and tom thinks he knows  the exact point where they knew he'd be  a great malfoy  he spent the entire audition pretending  like he was a fan of the books  so when the producers asked him what his  favorite scene was he had no choice but  to lie  the guy next to me said something about  gringotts and goblins i was just like  yeah  the producers must have taken that as a  very draco thing to do  and he got the part ivana lynch being in  the harry potter franchise was fate  and you can't convince us otherwise  before she even auditioned for the role  she had been pen pals with jk rowling  who encouraged her to overcome her  eating disorder  so when she heard there would be an open  audition for luna in london  she flew over with her father and waited  hours with thousands of other girls  after being screened on her looks take a  listen to what she told casting agents  and i was like if you don't pick me  that's okay that's your choice but  you're gonna be wrong  when they called in the actual casting  director to come in during her audition  she knew things had gone well and she  was right  just three days later they called her  back for a second audition  the rest is history we became well pen  friends  before i got the role bonnie wright has  her brother to thank for landing the  role of ginny weasley  she had only been nine years old at the  time of the harry potter casting  and her older brother was a huge fan of  the series so when he mentioned to her  that she looked like jenny she decided  to read the books and absolutely  fell in love after begging her mother to  get her an audition for jenny she got  the role  and here we are almost two decades later  i mean i started when i was nine i think  i don't know i think you can still  vividly remember  quite a lot of it james and oliver also  attended an open audition together  and continued to get called back until  landing the role but the funny thing was  they had no idea who was playing which  weasley twin  so they got to set the first day still  not knowing  and after getting their scripts they  finally decided it was time to ask the  casting director  except she had no idea either she  eventually came back with an answer  but james and oliver are convinced they  decided who would play who on a whim  tom felton wasn't the only one who had  no idea what or who  harry potter was devin murray's harry  potter audition had a pretty  embarrassing twist to it  after being invited to a screen test for  the first film he walked straight past  daniel to director chris columbus and  said  hi harry nice to meet you we're pretty  sure chris laughed it off considering he  was later offered the part  not to be dramatic but it would probably  be a crime against humanity if helena  bottom carter wasn't bellatrix  but that was almost a reality did my  research because i just thought  dude i didn't quite extend as far as  reading all the books  she wasn't the original actress cast for  the role they originally brought on  helen mcrory  but helen left the role after she found  out she was pregnant and they brought on  helena  the two ended up playing sisters helen  mcrory was recast as narcissa malfoy in  the last three films  the original dumbledore was played by  the iconic richard harris before he  sadly passed  away but we were so close to never  seeing his version of dumbledore  the producers offered him the role  multiple times and each time  offered him more money but richard just  didn't want to spend his golden years  working on a franchise  but he eventually gave in for that we  have his granddaughter to thank  who hilariously told her grandfather  she'd never speak to him again if he  didn't take on the role  alan rickman wasn't the first choice for  snape let that sink in  allen was only brought on after tim roth  turned down the role to take on the  blockbuster hit  planet of the apes at least it worked  out for both of them  we have to say we're very glad they  decided to go the route of alan rickman  just look at how much he loved the  franchise  i won't really miss anything because  it's been such an extraordinarily  complete  character to play rae finds originally  thought that voldemort just  wasn't his cup of tea he was a  classically trained actor  and couldn't see himself playing the  character but his sister talked some  sense into him  and we got the dark masterpiece that is  voldemort  honestly his theater training made  voldemort that much more dramatic  and we love it being the author of the  series  jk rowling of course had some names  swirling around her mind when it came to  casting  and robbie coltrane was one of them she  hand-picked him for the role of hagrid  and said he was the perfect choice  how could anyone argue with that luckily  he agreed and  absolutely loved his experience working  on the films  i think it's great it's it's a great  feeling gary oldman may have been the  perfect serious black  but his original motive behind getting  the role wasn't because he loved the  franchise  he simply needed the money to support  his family i needed the work  that's the honest answer honestly  respect  after getting the role and filming  prisoner of azkaban he fell in love with  the series alongside his kids  it's hard to believe that we were this  close from getting an entirely different  harry potter cast  it makes us even more glad that our fave  actors got the parts  even if they were in very unconventional  ways  what audition story is your favorite  let's chat about it below  we'd love it if you hit that subscribe  button and give this video a thumbs up  see you later potterheads

